# agent.suite — the flows an AI operator can drive, in one world.
#
# Run it with `--driver agent`: an operator on node1 performs each flow from
# its prompt.md — the lab's in a VM world where netsim runs, else one in
# node1's Docker container — and the same oracles that judge the scripted
# runs judge these. The tests continue one another's world, so this is one
# series against one world rather than a build per test. docker-agent.suite
# holds the operator flows that run only in Docker worlds.
#
# smoke is absent on purpose: it is a connectivity probe, not a flow anyone
# would ask an operator to perform, and it ships no prompt.md. The planner
# runs expel-node last on its own: it destroys its world.
bootstrap-user-software-key
adopt-node
blueprints-two-node
object-store
object-store-peer
read-remote-peer
read-swarm
expel-node
claimed-node-keeps-owner
